diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index c96e016..f06acb8 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -228,7 +228,9 @@ The status pane (top right) lists workers live. Click it to focus it, then:
 | `-` | clear the viewer |
 | `r` / `t` | read its last reply / its context packet in a popup |
 | `x` | kill it (asks first) |
-| `c` | archive killed workers |
+| `c` | archive workers whose pane is gone, then run `tp-clean --retired` |
+
+The pane holds at most `status.max_rows` rows (default 50, in `config/orchestration.json`). Every starting, working, needs-input, paused or `settled` worker is always shown, past the cap; the rest of the rows go to the newest finished workers, and a footer line, `N finished not shown (tp-agent find / tp-task list --all)`, says how many are left out. `tp-clean --retired` archives the finished workers that nothing can still ask for: completed (collected), stopped, killed or failed, finished more than `status.retire_after_minutes` ago (default 30), or, for a lane step, whose step the lane has closed. It closes only a dead pane of such a worker, never a live one, and prints `archived N, kept M` with the reasons for the first few it kept. A worker stays while a review of it is unfinished, a queued `after` or a retry names it as parent, a lane step is open, or a request of its own is pending or unreadable. `status.auto_retire` (default `true`) lets the status pane run that pass in the background once a minute; set it to `false` to run it only by hand or with `c`. A failed pass shows in the footer until one succeeds. A bad `status` value in the config is refused, not guessed at.
 
 States come from each worker's reporter: `starting`, `working`, `tool`, `waiting`, `permission`, `error`, then `done`, `failed:<code>` or `killed` once the process ends. A second line shows elapsed time and turns, and settled work shows its `result.md` path; a reply with no `RESULT_STATUS:` line shows as `paused`, not settled, and is listed under `paused` in the session index. The line is `RESULT_STATUS: complete` (or `empty`, `blocked`, `incomplete`) on a line of its own; Markdown around it (`### `, `**…**`, backticks, a list marker) is accepted, any other text before it on the line is not. One reader (`lib/result_status.py`) serves `collect`, `tp-review`, the verdict reader and the dispatcher; the paused notice from `collect` states this form and the `tp-agent message` command that asks the worker for it. Token counts include cached input; cost is shown only for Pi providers that price tokens. If the pane looks stale, see `/refresh-status` above.
 
